-- NUMBERS KEEP
--
-- A tower of six floors. Every floor is one section of the summer work for finishing year nine,
-- and every creature on it asks the kind of question that section asks.
--
-- Two things make this practice rather than a test:
--
--   You never move past a question you got wrong. It comes back until you get it right, and only
--   then does the floor start over. A floor is beaten by four in a row, first time, with no help.
--
--   Every question type has one named rule, shown the same way every single time, so that the
--   shape of it sticks. At the end the game writes your notes out to a file for you to copy.
--
-- Written in PoliteLang by Creeperdiamonds Studios.


please use "parts/questions.polite"


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The tower
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

please:
    show ""
    show "================================================================"
    show "                        N U M B E R S   K E E P"
    show "================================================================"
    show ""
    show "  Six floors. One for every section of your summer work."
    show ""
    show "  Four right in a row beats a floor. Get one wrong and you do"
    show "  that question again until it is right, and then the floor"
    show "  starts over. That is the whole point: you leave knowing it."
    show ""
    show "  Every rule you meet goes into your notes at the end."
    show ""
thank you for everything

please remember health is 20
please remember hits is 0
please remember misses is 0
please remember best is 0
please remember book is an empty lookup
please remember floor is 1

please repeat until floor is over 7:
    show ""
    show "----------------------------------------------------------------"
    check if floor is over 6:
        show "  THE TOP OF THE TOWER   --   {the name of floor with floor}"
    otherwise:
        show "  FLOOR {floor}   --   {the name of floor with floor}"
    thanks
    show "----------------------------------------------------------------"
    show ""

    remember needed is 4
    check if floor is over 6:
        change needed to 5
    thanks

    remember streak is 0
    change health to 20

    keep going forever:
        check if streak is at least needed:
            stop repeating
        thanks

        remember q is a question for with floor
        remember text is item 1 of q or ""
        remember answer is the number in (item 2 of q or "0") or 0
        remember working is item 3 of q or ""
        remember which is the number in (item 4 of q or "1") or 1
        remember creature is item 5 of q or "thing"

        remember rule is the rule named with which
        remember rulename is item 1 of rule or ""
        remember ruletext is item 2 of rule or ""
        remember hebrew is item 3 of rule or ""

        -- Every rule is written into the book the first time it is met.
        check if not (book knows about rulename):
            put "{ruletext}\n     ({hebrew})" for rulename in book
        thanks

        show ""
        show "  The {creature} bars the stair.   [ you {health} ]   [ {streak} of {needed} ]"
        show ""
        show "    {text}"
        show ""

        ask "  Your answer?  " as given

        check if given is answer:
            add 1 to hits
            add 1 to streak
            check if streak is over best:
                change best to streak
            thanks
            check if streak is at least 3:
                show ""
                show "  RIGHT -- and that is {streak} in a row. The {creature} reels."
            otherwise:
                show ""
                show "  Right. The {creature} gives ground."
            thanks
        otherwise:
            add 1 to misses
            show ""
            show "  Not this time. The answer was {answer}."
            show ""
            show "  THE RULE:  {rulename}"
            show "             {ruletext}"
            show "             ({hebrew})"
            show ""
            show "  The way to it:"
            show "{working}"
            show ""
            show "  Now do that one again, and this time it will stay with you."
            show ""

            -- You do not walk past a question you got wrong.
            keep going forever:
                show "    {text}"
                show ""
                ask "  Your answer?  " as again
                check if again is answer:
                    show ""
                    show "  Yes. That is it, and now it is yours."
                    stop repeating
                thanks
                show ""
                show "  Not yet. Remember: {rulename}"
                show "                     {ruletext}"
                show ""
            thank you for repeating

            take 5 from health
            change streak to 0
            show ""
            show "  The {creature} strikes while you were working it out."
            show "  The floor starts over."

            check if health is at most 0:
                show ""
                show "  You sit down on the step and get your breath back."
                show "  Nothing is lost. Begin the floor again."
                change health to 20
            thanks
        thank you for checking
    thank you for repeating

    show ""
    show "  The way up is clear."
    add 1 to floor
thank you for repeating


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- What you take away
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

please show ""
please show "================================================================"
please show "  YOU REACHED THE TOP."
please show "================================================================"
please show ""
please show "  Right first time:  {hits}"
please show "  Had to go again:   {misses}"
please show "  Longest run:       {best}"
please show ""

please remember notes is "NUMBERS KEEP -- the rules you met\n"
please add "==================================\n\n" to notes
please add "Copy these into your book. They are the whole of it.\n\n" to notes

please remember counted is 0
please for every name in the keys of book:
    add 1 to counted
    add "{counted}. {name}\n" to notes
    add "     {the value for name in book or ""}\n\n" to notes
thank you for repeating

please add "\nRight first time: {hits}     Had to go again: {misses}     Longest run: {best}\n" to notes

please show "  Your notes:"
please show ""
please show notes

please try to:
    write notes to "numbers-keep-notes.txt"
    show "  Written to numbers-keep-notes.txt as well, ready to copy out."
otherwise if it does not work out:
    show "  I could not write the file, because {what went wrong}."
    show "  The notes are above all the same."
thank you for trying

please show ""
